            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0914" n="810" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg810"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Woodward Electoral Mission/124: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-16T16:00:00-05:45">July 16, 1932—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. Legation’s telegram 124, July 15, 9 a.m. Contract for sale of gasoline
                    storage tank in Corinto to West India Oil Company was approved by Congress
                    yesterday. Balance of sale price, approximately $10,000, will probably be paid
                    to Government sometime next week. I intend to discuss with President Moncada tomorrow the possibility of securing
                    from this source additional funds urgently needed by the Electoral Mission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
